  ▸ LR SCHEDULE: per step, tf-models CosineDecay over every step of the 100 epochs counted from step 0 (floor 0.000000), LinearWarmup 0→cosine(5 ep) over 5 epochs on top; the step 0-based
  ▸ STOCHASTIC DEPTH: 18 drop sites, keeps #[0.988000, 0.983000, 0.980000, 0.977000, 0.974000, 0.971000, 0.968000, 0.965000, 0.960000, 0.957000, 0.954000, 0.951000, 0.948000, 0.945000, 0.942000, 0.939000, 0.937000, 0.934000] — host-drawn per step, 1/keep folded in, NOT on the resident path. Eval is the identity (drop-free forward).
  ▸ CLASSIFIER DROPOUT: keep 0.800000, mask tensor<512x1280xf32> (PER-ELEMENT, one Bernoulli per example×feature — not per-example like the drop scales), host-drawn per step at seed+999983, 1/keep folded in. Eval is the identity (drop-free forward).
  ▸ GRADIENT ACCUMULATION: k = 8, blob region 3 of 4 [θ|m|v|G]. Micro-batch 512 x 8 = EFFECTIVE BATCH 4096. 2496 micro-batches/epoch = 312 updates/epoch; the LR schedule and Adam's bias correction run on UPDATES, the augmentation and the prefetch on micro-batches.
  eval batch 64 (the batch @mnv4in256_fwd_eval was RENDERED at) != train batch 128 — sound because eval is class-batch-independent
